diff --git a/saas/README.md b/saas/README.md
index 28b0891..95ead5e 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -105,3 +105,40 @@ knife ssh 'hostname:fizzy-lb-*' 'sudo docker exec fizzy-load-balancer kamal-prox
 ## License
 
 fizzy-saas is released under the [O'Saasy License](LICENSE.md).
+
+### Hosted billing configuration
+
+Billing is enabled only in SaaS mode. Configure these variables before enabling
+checkout:
+
+* `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`
+* `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (the signing secret for this endpoint/environment)
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID`: a recurring USD $20/month price for Unlimited
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID`: a recurring USD $25/month price for Unlimited+
+
+Enable Stripe's hosted customer portal with subscription changes between those
+prices and cancellation. Register `POST /stripe/webhooks` (without an account
+URL prefix) for `customer.subscription.created`, `customer.subscription.updated`,
+and `customer.subscription.deleted`. Apply the SaaS database migrations before
+deploying. No Stripe connection is needed to boot the app or run its tests.
+
+The Free plan includes 1,000 published cards and 1 GB of storage. Drafts do not
+consume the card allowance; the existing `cards_count` column remains the card
+numbering sequence, not billing usage. Unlimited includes unlimited cards and
+5 GB; Unlimited+ includes unlimited cards and 500 GB. Existing explicit storage
+exceptions are preserved. Active and trialing subscriptions grant paid access;
+canceling at period end keeps access until Stripe ends the subscription. Checkout
+redirects do not grant access: signed subscription webhooks do.
+
+Staff can use `/admin/accounts` to comp an account (Unlimited without payment),
+uncomp it, override its measured card/storage usage, or reset the override.
+Comping does not change an existing Stripe subscription or reduce Unlimited+
+storage. Blank override fields use measured usage; Reset removes the override
+entirely. These support actions do not change card numbering or storage records.
+
+The billing tests stub all outbound Stripe requests and sign webhook payloads
+locally. Run them, including the quota and support tests, with:
+
+```sh
+CI=1 SAAS=true DATABASE_ADAPTER=sqlite PARALLEL_WORKERS=1 bin/rails test saas/test
+```
diff --git a/saas/app/controllers/account/billing/checkouts_controller.rb b/saas/app/controllers/account/billing/checkouts_controller.rb
